### Summary

No new findings in this part. The deferred color upgrade now has its own marker and only writes when the folder still holds the old Default and rose. It also yields to changes made on another Mac and to local edits. The same-folder relocate shortcut, the pendingInit relocate case and the uncertain-result messages all match their tests. Of the open threads, only the one about relocating the active workspace dropping pending captures is still open. I did not check the `different`-identity pendingInit relocate case beyond the registry code I read.

<details><summary>What the change connects to (3 closed, 0 open)</summary>

Questions the reviewer answered about what this change does to the running product. The engine checked that the cited lines exist, not that the answers are true.

**Closed, with the lines they rest on**
- Deferred color upgrade written on reconnect only if the folder still holds the old Default and rose (`apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:681`) — A Default changed on another Mac while this folder was away is no longer overwritten. If it fails: A write failure is swallowed and the marker stays, so the next probe retries. Evidence: `apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:661-709`.
- Picking the workspace's current folder in Change folder returns early (`apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/relocate.ts:39`) — No remount or save prompt on a no-op pick. If it fails: checkRelocate runs first, so a refusal still surfaces. Evidence: `apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/relocate.ts:36-46`.
- Rejected create, edit and relocate IPC calls show an 'uncertain' message (`apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspace-dialog.tsx:130`) — Visible message that tells the user to check before retrying. If it fails: None found. Evidence: `apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspace-dialog.tsx:127-151`, `apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspaces-context.tsx:172-181`.

